/*
 * diag_head - the header comment of a diagnose source: where the file came from (the old signatures' block).
 *
 * The owner: "the comment of the diagnose should keep metadata like the signatures did: file name, checksum, date modified".
 * The old block (Generated by KOFViewer / Test sample / Researcher / Created, updated / Engine) is written by kof_dsrc_head
 * (libkofeng/databases/diagsrc.c) and Save puts it in front of every file it creates.
 *
 * PINNED: the block (name + sha256, researcher when given, created/updated, engine constants) and what is not known is absent;
 * a refresh keeps Created and moves updated; a comment that is not the tool's is untouched; kof_dsrc_patch keeps the block; Save
 * writes it from the object (and nothing about a sample with no object); Save again and a hand-headed file are not rewritten; the
 * builder gives byte-identical artifacts with the header, without it and under a hand header.
 *
 * Why the old tests missed it: (a) nothing wrote a header, so no row could ask for one; (b) the Save tests read a file back
 * through the reader and compared declarations, never the text above the first declaration, and no row built a diagnose twice
 * to compare the packs.
 */

